- op: discuss  # ecd7
  at: '2026-04-20T14:10:48Z'  # ecd7
  by: agent  # ecd7
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ecd7
  clock: 5  # ecd7
  nonce: ecd7  # ecd7
  message: "Slice D landed in PR #3229 (merged to dev as ede081e2f). TrackerApp now compiles the item-ID pattern once at __init__ via build_item_id_pattern(tracker_set.config), exposes _item_exists as the resolver (ItemNotFoundError/AmbiguousPrefixError → absent, so dead/ambiguous IDs render as plain text), and pre-processes each pane's markup through _apply_nav_hotspots before Static.update(). The three _show_* methods (_show_detail, _show_std_detail, _show_activity) now wrap rendered text so item IDs become [@click=jump_to_item(...)] hotspots. action_jump_to_item pushes ItemNavModal (delivered in slice C3) with exists/content_for/id_pattern injection; _nav_modal_content_for reuses _format_detail_lines + _format_activity_lines so in-modal content matches the originating context (design constraint 4). Defensive no-op when the clicked ID no longer resolves (race with delete). 10 new tests in test_tui_item_nav_integration.py cover the resolver (known / unknown / ambiguous prefix), the hotspot wrap (resolvable wrapped, unresolvable left plain, empty no-op), the content-for pair, and Pilot end-to-end checks (cross-ref rendering, modal push on action, unknown-ID no-op). 5 snapshot SVGs regenerated to reflect the item-own-ID underline now shown in detail view. 100% coverage verified via check-package-coverage tracker. All WI-sulij design constraints satisfied: (1) config-driven prefixes via build_item_id_pattern, (2) no dead hotspots, (4) modal mirrors right-side panes via shared formatting helpers, (5) non-persistent history scoped to the modal via slice C3's NavigationHistory."  # ecd7
